Pac-Man (Atari 8-bit) - preservation and C port
================================================

What the MIT licence in LICENSE covers
  The work of this project: the C port (src/c), the Python analysis and test
  tools (tools, tests), the documentation (docs, analysis) and the build files.

What it does NOT cover
  1. The original game. "Pac-Man" and the Atari 8-bit cartridge program are the
     property of their owners. src/asm/pacman.s is a disassembly of that
     program, kept for preservation and study; the MIT licence gives no right
     in the original code, only in this project's own annotations and tooling.
     The cartridge ROM itself is NOT part of this release.
  2. The Atari operating system ROMs. Not part of this release.
  3. Third-party material under third-party/, each under its own licence:
       EightBit Atari-Regular font (Steve Boswell, 2018), SIL Open Font
       License 1.1: third-party/EightBit-Atari-Fonts/OFL.txt. The licence and
       credit must stay with every copy. See third-party/README.md for the
       provenance note.

What you must supply
  A legally obtained copy of the Pac-Man Atari 8-bit cartridge ROM, placed at
  original/Pac-Man.rom. The port reads its non-code data (maze, character
  sets, tables) from it when it starts; nothing derived from the ROM is
  shipped (resources/ is rebuilt on your machine, never distributed).

Build and verification instructions: docs/63-build-and-dependencies.md and
docs/65-release.md.
